# fixedbugs, defect 582, lane b19-pack, 2026-10-10, a shape beside
# `fixedbugs-582-a-header-s-unclosed-pack-push-leaves-two-modules-one-record-layout`:
# Apple's `#pragma options align=packed`, which clang keeps on the same
# stack as `pack`, packed `main`'s records on this Mac the same way. Where
# the target has no `options` pragma, clang ignores it in the header's
# region, and the records have their layout either way.

use fixedbugs582/pair

extern "fixedbugs-582-a-header-s-options-align-packed-leaves-the-records-their-layout.h"
    function llabs(x: i64) -> i64

function main()
    p = pair.make(llabs(-123456789))
    print(p.b, " ", pair.second(p), " ", pair.second(pair.Pair(a: 2, b: llabs(-987654321))))
    print(pair.area(pair.shape(llabs(-7))))
